  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying the least probable outcome (minimum probability event) in each lottery and comparing their payoffs. Lottery B has the least probable outcome (0.1% vs. 0.2%), and since its payoff is higher, the reason would select B. The individual also selects the lottery with the higher payoff (6000), acknowledging the lower probability but dismissing it as negligible. While the individual does not explicitly frame their reasoning in terms of 'least probable outcome,' they do focus on the rarest winning event and prefer the one with the better payoff. The justification aligns with the logic of the decision reason, even if not articulated in identical terms. The core of the reasoning—favoring the better outcome among very low-probability events—is present. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason, albeit implicitly.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

