{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes—the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability in each lottery. For Lottery A, the most favorable outcome is 0 Euros with a probability of 55%, which is not the least probable outcome (since 55% is higher than 45%). The least probable outcome in A is -6000 Euros (45%). For Lottery B, the most favorable outcome is 0 Euros with 10% probability, which is indeed the least probable outcome (minimum probability). The reason compares the most favorable outcomes among the least probable ones. In this case, the least probable outcomes are: -6000 (45%) for A and 0 (10%) for B. The more favorable of these two is 0 Euros (from B). Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B because its least probable outcome (0 Euros) is more favorable than that of A (-6000 Euros).",
