  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates the most favorable outcome among the least probable outcomes of each lottery and prefers the one with the better such outcome. As established, this would favor Lottery B (least probable outcome is 0 Euros at 10%) over A (least probable outcome is -6000 at 45%). However, the individual focuses on the higher probability of avoiding loss (55% in A vs 10% in B) and explicitly prefers A for that reason. They are attending to the most probable favorable outcome, not the least probable one. Therefore, their reasoning runs contrary to the logic of the decision reason, which emphasizes rare events. There is no indication that the individual considered the least probable outcomes; instead, they emphasize the relative certainty of outcomes. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
