{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, i.e., the outcome with the minimum probability in each. For Lottery A, the least probable outcome is -3000 Euros with a probability of 0.2%. For Lottery B, the least probable outcome is -6000 Euros with a probability of 0.1%. The reason compares these least probable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less negative) such outcome. Since -3000 is more favorable than -6000, the reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the decision reason is applicable to this decision problem, and it would lead to a preference for Lottery A based on comparing the least probable outcomes.",
