{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcome of each lottery, defined as the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability. For Lottery A, the outcomes are 1000€ (50%) and 0€ (50%). The most favorable outcome is 1000€, which has a probability of 50%. For Lottery B, the outcome is 500€ with 100% probability. The most favorable outcome is 500€, with a probability of 100%. The least probable outcome in Lottery A is 1000€ (50%), and in Lottery B, it is 500€ (100%). Since 50% < 100%, the least probable outcome in A has lower probability than in B. Therefore, the reason compares the most favorable outcomes associated with the minimum probabilities: 1000€ (from A) vs. 500€ (from B). Since 1000€ > 500€, the reason would prefer Lottery A.",
